(7760638, 1285305, 68504, '<td valign="top">very annoying. what is the point of this art nouveau ascension?<br/>eta: didn''t mean to sound so negative: it is a fine photo; I totally miss the point of much of modern architecture, although one might similarly have missed the point of a lot of traditional church architecture. the question remains: where do the stairs lead?<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2023-12-04 00:15:55.</i></td>', 'very annoying. what is the point of this art nouveau ascension?eta: didn''t mean to sound so negative: it is a fine photo; I totally miss the point of much of modern architecture, although one might similarly have missed the point of a lot of traditional church architecture. the question remains: where do the stairs lead?', '2023-12-03 22:43:47.000000', '2023-12-04 00:15:55.000000', 1),
(7760641, 1285305, 114285, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by tnun:</b></div><hr/><i> very annoying. what is the point of this art nouveau ascension?<br/>eta: didn''t mean to sound so negative: it is a fine photo; I totally miss the point of much of modern architecture, although one might similarly have missed the point of a lot of traditional church architecture. the question remains: where do the stairs lead? </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>The stairs lead to another platform. So they are not pointless :)</td>', 'Originally posted by tnun: very annoying. what is the point of this art nouveau ascension?eta: didn''t mean to sound so negative: it is a fine photo; I totally miss the point of much of modern architecture, although one might similarly have missed the point of a lot of traditional church architecture. the question remains: where do the stairs lead?   The stairs lead to another platform. So they are not pointless :)', '2023-12-04 00:23:49.000000', NULL, 0),
